Another thing I'd like changed is the number of wands. There are just too
many of them, even if I don't run into a bones file and immediately double
the quantity.

How about making wands *much* rarer, but increasing the number and power
of charging scrolls? This makes sense: a Wand of Magic Missiles should
compare to a machine gun that can be reloaded, not a pocket of fire crackers
that can each be used only once.

This change would mean that your game style would be affected by the wands
you can find. Finding a wand of fire would be an exciting event, not just
another wand that you have to carry so that monsters don't pick it up. 

Oh yes - amulets. I'm sick of weedy little monsters with Amulets of Life
Saving. Either introduce a pick-pocket command (depends on dexterity,
rogues get a plus) or make the AoLS susceptible to falling off your neck.
This would add more excitement - if a monster drops it you scream and
leap; if you drop it you just scream.

